            <ArticleTitle>[Thrombophlebitis of the ovarian vein. Apropos of 2 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>717-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thrombophlebitis of the ovarian vein is a rare post-partum complication. Its diagnosis is said to be difficult, but was greatly facilitated by the progress made in imaging. The authors report about two cases identified with computed tomography. Evolution was favorable in both cases with an anticoagulant and antibiotic treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
